          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "накануне (nakanúne) — \"the day before, on the eve\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Накануне свадьбы она не спала. Nakanúne svádby oná ne spalá. On the eve of the wedding she did not sleep."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With the genitive: накануне (nakanúne) праздника — on the eve of the holiday. Alone it means \"the day before\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "накануне (nakanúne) is built on на \"on\" and канун \"the eve of a feast\", which is usually traced to Greek kanṓn \"a rule\", the name of a church service sung on the eve; EtymDB lists no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
