              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "прежде (prézhde) — \"before, formerly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Прежде здесь был маленький парк. Prézhde zdes byl málenkiy park. Formerly there was a small park here."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Прежде чем + infinitive — before doing: прежде (prézhde) чем уйти. Прежде всего — first of all."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "прежде (prézhde) is a Church Slavonic word, prěžde \"before\" (EtymDB), with the -ре- of the church language; the native Russian shape of the same root is перед \"in front of\"."
            }
          ]
        },
