              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "спустя (spustyá) — \"later, after (a stretch of time)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Спустя два года они снова встретились. Spustyá dva góda oní snóva vstrétilis. Two years later they met again."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With the accusative of time, before or after it: спустя (spustyá) неделю or неделю спустя (spustyá) — a week later."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "спустя (spustyá) is an old adverbial participle of спустить \"to let down\", built on пустить \"to let go\", inherited from Proto-Slavic pustiti (EtymDB): time let go by."
            }
          ]
        },
